{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadChainVolume","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadChainVolume","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolumeSqueeze","lean:module:QOU.Knot.CatalanValueBounds"],"declarations":29,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.volumeConjectureWhiteheadChain_proved","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.volumeConjectureWhiteheadChain_proved","kind":"instance","line":895,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadChainVolume.lean#L895-L897","doc":"The proved instance — machine-checked (W1–W5), no sorry. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.VolumeConjectureWhiteheadChain.limit_eq_vol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.VolumeConjectureWhiteheadChain.limit_eq_vol","kind":"theorem","line":889,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadChainVolume.lean#L889-L889","doc":"`(2π/(2M+1))·log P_M → 4·Cl₂(π/2) = 4G` as `M → ∞`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.VolumeConjectureWhiteheadChain.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.VolumeConjectureWhiteheadChain.mk","kind":"ctor","line":887,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadChainVolume.lean#L887-L887","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.VolumeConjectureWhiteheadChain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.VolumeConjectureWhiteheadChain","kind":"class","line":882,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadChainVolume.lean#L882-L893","doc":"**The Whitehead-chain per-link volume-conjecture carrier**, mirroring\n`VolumeConjecture41` / `VolumeConjectureBorromean`: the single content\nfield is the limit identity for the `W_{a,2,1,0}` chain (volume\n`4G = Vol(𝓑₃)/2`, one regular ideal octahedron).  The instance below is\na genuine sorry-free proof (bricks W1–W5), not a citation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.tendsto_log_whiteheadKashaev_vol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.tendsto_log_whiteheadKashaev_vol","kind":"theorem","line":859,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadChainVolume.lean#L859-L880","doc":"**The Whitehead-chain volume-conjecture instance, machine-proved (W5).**\n`(2π/N)·log P_M → 4·Cl₂(π/2) = 4G = 8Λ(π/4) = Vol(W_{a,2,1,0})` along\nthe odd orders `N = 2M+1` — the third in-repo volume-conjecture\ninstance after 4₁ and the Borromean rings, and the value shared with\nthe Whitehead link proper (one regular ideal octahedron).  The carrier\n`P_M` is vdV Lemma 1's phase-free positive sum; by the exact modulus\nidentity `|J_N(W_{a,b,c,d})| = N^b · P_M^{c+d}` (`b ≥ 2`) the invariant-\nlevel rate differs only by the vanishing `(2π/N)·b·log N`.  See the\nfile header for the carrier's epistemic status. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.tendsto_two_pi_log_whiteheadKashaev","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.tendsto_two_pi_log_whiteheadKashaev","kind":"theorem","line":623,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadChainVolume.lean#L623-L857","doc":"**Whitehead brick W5b — the squeeze (sorry-free).**  Along the odd\nroot-of-unity orders `N = 2M+1`, the scaled log of the Whitehead-chain\npositive sum tends to the octahedron volume:\n`(2π/N)·log P_M → 4·Cl₂(π/2) = 4G`.  Upper envelope: at most `M+1 ≤ N`\nterms, each below the W5a ceiling; lower envelope: the single grid term\nat `k* = ⌊N/4⌋` (the `y = π/4` saddle), whose W4b deviation target\nconverges to the saddle value by continuity of `clausen`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadTerm_ceiling","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadTerm_ceiling","kind":"theorem","line":464,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadChainVolume.lean#L464-L618","doc":"**Whitehead brick W5a — the per-term ceiling (sorry-free).**  For every\n`k ≤ M` at `N = 2M+1`, the scaled log-term is at most the continuum\nsaddle value plus the vanishing slack and deviation:\n\n    (2π/N)·log S_{M,k} ≤ 4·Cl₂(π/2) + whiteheadSlack N + 10·masterErr N.\n\nFor `1 ≤ k`: the W4b deviation lands on `2Ψ(k) = WF(kπ/N) −\n4·(log-sine half-cell) + clausen(2Mπ/N)`, bounded by the W5a-max plus the\nslack.  For `k = 0`: `log S_{M,0} = s_M` directly, one deviation\ninstance plus the endpoint `clausen` value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.tendsto_whiteheadSlack","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.tendsto_whiteheadSlack","kind":"theorem","line":417,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadChainVolume.lean#L417-L461","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadSlack_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadSlack_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":408,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadChainVolume.lean#L408-L415","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadSlack","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadSlack","kind":"def","line":401,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadChainVolume.lean#L401-L406","doc":"The Whitehead grid-to-continuum slack: one half-grid log-sine cell (the\n`π/N` offset between `2Mπ/N` and `π` inside the shifted `clausen`) plus\nthe endpoint `clausen` value near `π`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadFunctional_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadFunctional_le","kind":"theorem","line":316,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadChainVolume.lean#L316-L399","doc":"**Whitehead brick W5a-max — the continuum max (sorry-free).**  On\n`[0, π/2]` the functional never exceeds its saddle value `4·Cl₂(π/2)`,\nattained at `y = π/4`: compactness gives a maximiser; the boundary\nvalues vanish while the saddle value is positive; the interior critical\nequation `2 sin(y + π/2) = 2 sin y` forces `cos y = sin y`, hence\n`cos 2y = 0` with `2y ∈ (0, π)`, hence `y = π/4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadFunctional_quarter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadFunctional_quarter","kind":"theorem","line":300,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadChainVolume.lean#L300-L314","doc":"The saddle value: `WF(π/4) = 4·Cl₂(π/2)` — series bridge + antisymmetry. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadFunctional_pi_div_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadFunctional_pi_div_two","kind":"theorem","line":294,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadChainVolume.lean#L294-L298","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadFunctional_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadFunctional_zero","kind":"theorem","line":289,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadChainVolume.lean#L289-L292","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.hasDerivAt_whiteheadFunctional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.hasDerivAt_whiteheadFunctional","kind":"theorem","line":266,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadChainVolume.lean#L266-L287","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.continuous_whiteheadFunctional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.continuous_whiteheadFunctional","kind":"theorem","line":258,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadChainVolume.lean#L258-L264","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadFunctional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadFunctional","kind":"def","line":250,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadChainVolume.lean#L250-L256","doc":"The Whitehead-chain continuum functional in the half-angle variable\n`y = kπ/N`:  `WF(y) = 2·clausen(2y) − 2·clausen(2y + π)` — the limit of\nthe scaled log-term `(2π/N)·log S_{M,k}` along `k/N → y/π`, using\n`2Mπ/N → π` and `clausen π = 0`.  Simpler than the Borromean functional\n(no duplication step). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.abs_log_whiteheadTerm_deviation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.abs_log_whiteheadTerm_deviation","kind":"theorem","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadChainVolume.lean#L208-L246","doc":"**Whitehead brick W4b — the k-uniform deviation (sorry-free).**  For\n`1 ≤ k` and `k + M ≤ N − 1`, the scaled log-term deviates from the\nClausen-primitive combination\n\n    Ψ_N(k) = 2·(F((k+M)π/N) − F(kπ/N)) − F(Mπ/N),\n    F(x) = −clausen(2x)/2\n\nby at most `5·masterErr N` — coefficient sum `2+2+1` of the E5c-4\nk-uniform bound applied at the indices `k+M`, `k`, `M`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.log_whiteheadTerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.log_whiteheadTerm","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadChainVolume.lean#L140-L206","doc":"**Whitehead brick W4a — the log identity (sorry-free, exact).**  With the\nE4/E5 Riemann sums `s_m = Σ_{j∈Icc 1 m} log(2 sin(jπ/N))`,\n\n    log S_{M,k} = 2·(s_{k+M} − s_k) − s_M\n\n— the numerator window `(k, k+M]` splits off the prefix `[1, k]`, and the\nsquared factors contribute the `2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadTerm_le_whiteheadKashaev","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadTerm_le_whiteheadKashaev","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadChainVolume.lean#L129-L138","doc":"Single-term floor: each term bounds the sum below (the lower-envelope\nhook for the W5 squeeze). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadKashaev_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadKashaev_pos","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadChainVolume.lean#L117-L127","doc":"**The Whitehead-chain sum is positive** (`2M ≤ N − 1`, satisfied by the\nchain instance `N = 2M+1`) — `log` of it is well-defined, the floor the\nW5 squeeze stands on. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadTerm_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadTerm_pos","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadChainVolume.lean#L111-L115","doc":"Every term `S_{M,k}` with an in-grid window is strictly positive —\nno vanishing terms, no sign analysis (contrast the Borromean carrier). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadDen_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadDen_pos","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadChainVolume.lean#L101-L109","doc":"The denominator is positive for `M ≤ N − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadNum_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadNum_pos","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadChainVolume.lean#L90-L99","doc":"The numerator is positive whenever the window stays inside the grid\n(`k + M ≤ N − 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.sin_grid_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.sin_grid_pos","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadChainVolume.lean#L76-L88","doc":"Interior grid sines are positive: `0 < sin(jπ/N)` for `1 ≤ j ≤ N−1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadKashaev","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadKashaev","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadChainVolume.lean#L69-L74","doc":"The Whitehead-chain positive sum `P_M = Σ_{k=0}^{M} S_{M,k}` at\n`N = 2M+1` (the `N` parameter is kept general; the chain instance takes\n`N = 2M+1`).  By vdV Lemma 1 the invariant modulus is\n`|J_N(W_{a,b,c,d})| = N^b · P_M^{c+d}` for `b ≥ 2`, `N = 2M+1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadTerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadTerm","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadChainVolume.lean#L63-L67","doc":"One term of the Whitehead-chain Kashaev sum:\n`S_{M,k} = ∏_{j=1}^{M} 2 sin²((k+j)π/N)/sin(jπ/N)` (vdV Lemma 1),\nwritten as the reindexed quotient of `2 sin` products. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadDen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadDen","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadChainVolume.lean#L59-L61","doc":"Denominator of `S_{M,k}`: `∏_{j=1}^{M} 2 sin(jπ/N)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadNum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadNum","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadChainVolume.lean#L55-L57","doc":"Numerator of `S_{M,k}`: `∏_{j=k+1}^{k+M} (2 sin(jπ/N))²`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}